The `scheduling.init` call used to pass `apiUrl`, and this PR drops it. `post-scheduling/index.js` reads `options.apiUrl` inside `init = async (options) => ...`. With no argument, `options` is `undefined`, so the adapter throws a TypeError. Because this runs inside `Promise.all`, `initServices()` rejects and Ghost fails to start. Even if the TypeError were avoided, `PostScheduler` throws `IncorrectUsageError('post-scheduling: no apiUrl was provided')` when `apiUrl` is falsy.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="366-369"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The original `urlUtils.urlFor('api', {type: 'admin'}, true)` argument has to come back. Without it the scheduler cannot be constructed.

::suggestion{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="368-370"}
        scheduling.init({
            apiUrl: urlUtils.urlFor('api', {type: 'admin'}, true)
        }),

The PR removes `slack.listen()` from the `Promise.all` block. The description and commit are about xmlrpc, so this looks accidental. `slack.listen()` is the only thing that registers `slackListener` on `post.published` and the `slack.test` handler, and no other code calls it. After this change, Slack notifications for published posts and the Slack test button stop working. Nothing errors, so the regression would go unnoticed. The `slack` const on line 319 is also now unused.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="363-364"}

Restore `slack.listen()` in the parallel block. Keep the `slack` require, which is still needed for this call.

`emailAddressService.init()` was a sequential `await` before the parallel block. It is now the first element of `Promise.all`. This works today because `EmailAddressServiceWrapper.init()` is synchronous and array elements are evaluated left to right, so `this.service` is set before `emailService.init()` reads `emailAddressService.service` in `EmailServiceWrapper`. But the ordering guarantee is now implicit. The comment "newsletter service and email service depend on email address service" is left above a blank line, separated from the code it describes.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="349-352"}

Either keep the sequential `await emailAddressService.init();` before `Promise.all`, or move the comment so it sits next to the array entry and states that array order matters.

The PR description says "No other services or boot order affected" and checks "I've written an automated test". The only test change deletes the xmlrpc unit test. Nothing covers `initServices()`. The scheduling-signature break and the dropped `slack.listen()` would both have been caught by a boot smoke test or a unit test asserting that the slack listener is registered. The description is wrong about boot order, since `emailAddressService.init()` was moved and `slack.listen()` was dropped.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/boot.js" lines="351-368"}

Add a test that exercises `initServices()` (or the boot path that calls it) and asserts the scheduler receives an `apiUrl` and that the Slack listener is registered. Correct the PR description to list every change in the boot sequence.
